│    └─0 text "Repository architecture"
├─1  paragraph[11]
│    ├─0  text "Tastemaker is the definition of this repository's architecture. The structure, the files each\ndirectory holds and the checks they must pass are the Tastemaker specs, templates and rules of the\npackage "
│    ├─1  inlineCode "tastemaker/"
│    ├─2  text " ("
│    ├─3  inlineCode "idiomatic.arch"
│    ├─4  text ") and of each product's own "
│    ├─5  inlineCode "tastemaker/"
│    ├─6  text ", placed by each\n"
│    ├─7  inlineCode "tastemaker.toml"
│    ├─8  text ". Tastemaker's own design is in "
│    ├─9  inlineCode "crates/tastemaker/docs/README.md"
│    └─10 text "."
├─2  paragraph[1]
│    └─0 text "This file keeps only what those cannot express: the principles behind the specs, and the\nindex of the products' design documents."
├─3  heading[1]
│    │ depth: 2
│    └─0 text "A. Principles"
├─4  heading[1]
│    │ depth: 3
│    └─0 text "A.1 Levels"
├─5  paragraph[13]
│    ├─0  text "The levels (repository, workspace, crate, domain), the product layout and what each level is\nbuilt from are the specs of "
