│    ├─8  text ", "
│    ├─9  inlineCode "cli"
│    ├─10 text ", "
│    ├─11 inlineCode "sdk"
│    └─12 text "."
├─6  heading[1]
│    │ depth: 3
│    └─0 text "A.2 A domain is a hexagon"
├─7  paragraph[9]
│    ├─0 text "Every domain is a hex, wired only at entry points (a command, an SDK entry): the "
│    ├─1 inlineCode "nu-hex"
│    ├─2 text ",\n"
│    ├─3 inlineCode "use-case"
│    ├─4 text ", "
│    ├─5 inlineCode "port"
│    ├─6 text " and "
│    ├─7 inlineCode "adapter"
│    └─8 text " specs, with their rules."
├─8  heading[1]
│    │ depth: 3
│    └─0 text "A.3 Public interfaces"
├─9  paragraph[9]
│    ├─0 text "A consumer of a product names its SDK alone (the "
│    ├─1 inlineCode "sdk"
│    ├─2 text " spec). Named, not restated: the rules\nno-reexports, no-public-options, no-domain-aliases, private-checked-fields and\nno-json-in-process; rustc's "
│    ├─3 inlineCode "private_interfaces"
│    ├─4 text " and "
│    ├─5 inlineCode "unnameable_types"
│    ├─6 text "; and the\nnominal-interface lint in "
│    ├─7 inlineCode "tools/lints"
│    └─8 text " for interface types."
├─10 heading[1]
│    │ depth: 3
│    └─0 text "A.4 Testing and evidence"
├─11 paragraph[11]
│    ├─0  text "Test files are placed by the "
│    ├─1  inlineCode "crate"
│    ├─2  text ", "
│    ├─3  inlineCode "use-case"
│    ├─4  text ", "
│    ├─5  inlineCode "cli"
│    ├─6  text ", "
│    ├─7  inlineCode "sdk"
│    ├─8  text " and "
│    ├─9  inlineCode "language"
│    └─10 text " specs. A missing\ntool, a zero-test target or an unexecuted case is never success."
